---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="SpotBook — B2B Wholesale Platform | viknik.tech" description="SpotBook is a B2B wholesale platform co-built by Rutvik Gulhane: from a first production deployment for P10 Denim / MG Sales built in 15 days to a modular Spring Boot platform for apparel wholesalers.">

  <div class="project-hero">
    <div class="hero__gradient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="project-hero__content container">
      <div class="project-hero__badge-wrap">
        <span class="chapter-badge" style="color: var(--accent-violet); border-color: var(--accent-violet);">PROJECT 01</span>
        <span class="project-hero__date">Sep 2025 – Jun 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <img src="/stickers/tech_spring.svg" alt="Spring Boot" width="60" height="60" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1; filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1));" />
        <img src="/stickers/tech_postgres.svg" alt="PostgreSQL" width="60" height="60" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1; filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1));" />
        <img src="/stickers/tech_react.svg" alt="React" width="60" height="60" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1; filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1));" />
      </div>
      <h1 class="project-hero__title fade-in">SpotBook: B2B Wholesale Platform</h1>
      <p class="project-hero__subtitle fade-in">Co-Founder & Full-Stack Developer · From a first production deployment for P10 Denim / MG Sales to a modular Spring Boot platform for apparel manufacturers and wholesalers.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Key Stats Banner -->
  <section class="metrics-banner section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stats__grid stagger-children">
        <div class="stats__card glass">
          <span class="stats__value">₹9 Cr+</span>
          <span class="stats__label">Wholesale Bookings (~$1.1M)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__card glass">
          <span class="stats__value">15 Days</span>
          <span class="stats__label">Initial Production Build</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__card glass">
          <span class="stats__value">2 Seasons</span>
          <span class="stats__label">Live Expo Operations</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stats__card glass">
          <span class="stats__value">6</span>
          <span class="stats__label">Domain Modules</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Product Evolution -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">From Production Deployment to Platform</h2>
        <p class="lead-text">SpotBook began with a real client deployment: a mobile-first production order-management system built in approximately 15 days for P10 Denim / MG Sales ahead of a trade expo.</p>
        <p>That deployment handled QR/product workflows, real-time inventory and order operations, and expo-floor support. Across two expo seasons it supported more than ₹9 Cr in wholesale bookings. Later SpotBook work extended the product into the multi-tenant architecture and domain capabilities documented below.</p>
        <p>This distinction matters: the first deployment proved the production workflow; the later platform engineering added the broader modular architecture, tenant isolation, and wholesale-domain depth.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">
          <a href="#initial-deployment" class="btn btn--outline">See the Initial Deployment Details →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Initial Deployment Details -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="initial-deployment">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Initial Deployment: P10 Denim / MG Sales</h2>
        <p class="lead-text">
          The first SpotBook deployment was built for a real wholesale expo environment, where sales teams had to capture bulk orders quickly while stock was moving across booths, distributors, and visiting retailers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before the system, sales reps wrote order items manually on paper slips. During peak hours, two reps could unknowingly sell the same limited stock to different retailers, creating post-expo cancellations, distributor disputes, and no reliable real-time reporting for the manufacturer.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 15-day build turned that workflow into a mobile-first PWA designed for noisy expo floors and 5-inch phone screens.
        </p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>Role-based access:</strong> admin dashboard, sales-agent interface, distributor/customer flows, and manufacturer-level controls.</li>
          <li><strong>QR-led product lookup:</strong> staff could scan sample tags and immediately view product variants, stock levels, and order options.</li>
          <li><strong>Concurrency-safe checkout:</strong> DB-level pessimistic locking and stock validation prevented overbooking during simultaneous live orders.</li>
          <li><strong>Automated receipts:</strong> PDF/text receipts were generated and delivered through WhatsApp after order placement.</li>
          <li><strong>Live reporting:</strong> dashboards exposed revenue, order volume, inventory movement, and top-selling designs during expo days.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Initial Deployment Screenshots -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-heading fade-in" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">Initial Deployment Interfaces</h2>

      <div class="gallery-grid grid grid--2 fade-in">
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <img src="/media/dashboard.jpg" alt="SpotBook initial deployment admin dashboard" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="gallery-caption">Admin dashboard: real-time revenue and order tracking</p>
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-item">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <img src="/media/Product_catalog.jpg" alt="SpotBook initial deployment product catalog" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="gallery-caption">Product catalog: stock filtering and size-variant ordering</p>
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-item">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <img src="/media/BI_1.jpg" alt="SpotBook initial deployment inventory overview" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="gallery-caption">Inventory overview: top-selling designs and stock valuation</p>
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-item">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <img src="/media/BI_chart_1.jpg" alt="SpotBook initial deployment analytics chart" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="gallery-caption">Analytics: revenue trends during live expo operations</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Human Story Behind the Architecture -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Why SpotBook Exists</h2>
        <p class="lead-text">
          The initial SpotBook deployment proved the workflow for one manufacturer. During those 15 days at the expo, I sat across the table from 5 other manufacturers — and every conversation revealed the same pattern.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="spotbook-quote">
          "Business owners described what they <em>wanted</em>. Their salespeople and inventory managers described what they <em>actually needed</em>. Those were two very different products."
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          Warehouse staff didn't care about dashboards — they needed to know <strong>exactly how many pieces of Waist 32 × Dark Blue were left</strong> before promising them to a retailer. Salespeople didn't want a CRM — they wanted a POS that worked on a 5-inch phone in a noisy hall. Distributors didn't want login credentials — they wanted to browse a catalog via QR code without downloading anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's what shaped the zone architecture below. Every boundary exists because a real person on the expo floor had a different mental model of the same data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Architecture Overview -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Architectural Philosophy</h2>
        <p class="lead-text">
          Instead of jumping to microservices overhead for a 2-person team, SpotBook was built as a <strong>Modular Monolith</strong> with strict zone boundaries (Zones 0–7). Cross-module imports are restricted to explicit <code>api/</code> packages, keeping internals encapsulated — while preserving a clean future microservices migration path.
        </p>

        <div class="arch-box glass">
          <h3>Zone Boundaries (0 – 7)</h3>
          <ul class="zone-list">
            <li><strong>Zone 0: Control Plane (<code>backoffice</code>)</strong> — The <em>only</em> module that bypasses tenant filters.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 1: Identity (<code>iam</code>)</strong> — Multi-role authentication (5 roles) & tenant context management.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 2: Catalog (<code>catalog</code>)</strong> — Products, size matrices, prepacks, and pricing.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 3: Inventory (<code>inventory</code>)</strong> — Virtual stock calculation, warehouse locks, and reservations.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 4: Expo (<code>expo</code>)</strong> — Event sessions, booth QR allocations, and fast-order intake.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 5: Sales (<code>sales</code>)</strong> — Order processing, draft persistence, and fulfillment triggers.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 6: Fulfillment (<code>fulfillment</code>)</strong> — Packing, dispatch, and distributor receipts.</li>
            <li><strong>Zone 7: Platform (<code>platform</code>)</strong> — Shared event bus, auditing, and notifications.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-detail glass" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
          <h3>Multi-Tenant Isolation</h3>
          <p>Tenant filters are enforced at the Hibernate <code>@Filter</code> level — every query is automatically scoped to the authenticated manufacturer's <code>tenant_id</code>. Cross-tenant data access is structurally impossible outside Zone 0 (Backoffice). This was <strong>verified with integration tests</strong> that specifically attempt cross-tenant reads and assert 403/empty responses.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Features Grid -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-heading fade-in" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">Core Capabilities</h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid--2 fade-in">
        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">🔒</span>
          <h3>Multi-Tenant Data Isolation</h3>
          <p>Hibernate <code>@Filter</code>-based tenant scoping at the query level. Automatic isolation across all 6 domain modules — verified with integration tests that assert zero cross-tenant leakage.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">📊</span>
          <h3>Matrix Variant Ordering</h3>
          <p>Seamlessly handles 2D matrix orders (e.g. Waist Size 28-36 × 4 Denim Washes) with real-time stock validation and prepack bundle calculations.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">🔄</span>
          <h3>Surgical Order Editing</h3>
          <p>Identity-based diffing engine computes order deltas on edits. Backend uses <code>EDITING_RESERVED</code> transitional status with pessimistic inventory locking — preserving order identity without full teardown.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">⚡</span>
          <h3>Event-Driven Decoupling</h3>
          <p>Modules communicate asynchronously through Spring's internal event bus, avoiding direct cross-domain database coupling.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">🧪</span>
          <h3>TDD for Critical Paths</h3>
          <p>JUnit 5 + Mockito unit tests across all modules. Integration and regression tests on concurrency paths, stock delta validation, and tenant isolation — run before every expo deployment.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-card">
          <span class="capability-icon">👥</span>
          <h3>Architected for Multi-Dev Teams</h3>
          <p>Strict Zone boundaries (API vs. Internal packages) with Spring Modulith verification tests. Multiple developers can own separate domains without merge friction.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What I Learned -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">What I Learned</h2>
        
        <div class="lesson-grid">
          <div class="lesson-card">
            <h4>Architecture ≠ Diagrams</h4>
            <p>Zone boundaries aren't pretty lines on a whiteboard — they're enforced by <code>ApplicationModulesTest</code> failing your CI pipeline when someone sneaks a cross-module import. I learned that architecture only matters if it's testable.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lesson-card">
            <h4>Pragmatism > Purity</h4>
            <p>Modular monolith over microservices for a 2-person team wasn't compromise — it was the correct architecture for the team size, velocity constraints, and deployment complexity we had. The migration path to microservices is preserved in the zone contracts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lesson-card">
            <h4>Engineering ≠ Product</h4>
            <p>SpotBook's code was production-proven. The GTM strategy wasn't. Facebook ads collected garbage leads. Traditional wholesalers trust relationships, not forms. <strong>A software system without a dedicated sales engine cannot scale into a full business.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Business Reality / Honest Reflection -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="section-heading">The Business Reality</h2>
        <div class="honest-callout">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
            <h3>The GTM Lesson</h3>
            <img src="/stickers/no_corporate_filter.svg" alt="No Corporate Filter — Direct, honest communication and high engineering integrity" title="No Corporate Filter — Direct, honest communication and high engineering integrity" width="80" height="80" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1;" />
          </div>
          <p>
            While SpotBook's technical foundation was rock-solid and verified across 2 live expo deployments, the product faced distribution hurdles. Relying on paid digital marketing (Facebook lead ads) proved inefficient for a high-touch traditional industry.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Status:</strong> Paused — the product works, the engineering is proven. What stalled was go-to-market, not code quality. That distinction is important: this is an <em>engineering success</em> and a <em>distribution lesson</em>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Navigation Footer -->
  <section class="section section--alt" style="text-align: center;">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">Explore the Engineering</h3>
      <p style="font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        See the real production problems solved building SpotBook — concurrency bugs, race conditions, schema migrations, and deployment gauntlets.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/engineering" class="btn btn--primary">Read Engineering Challenges →</a>
        <a href="/story" class="btn btn--outline">Read The Full Story →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: calc(80px + var(--space-4xl)) 0 var(--space-3xl);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .project-hero .hero__gradient {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 20% 30%, rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.25), transparent 70%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 50% at 80% 20%, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.15), transparent 70%);
    animation: gradientShift 12s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  }

  .project-hero__content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .project-hero__badge-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .project-hero__date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .project-hero__title {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .project-hero__subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Stats */
  .stats__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .stats__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .stats__card {
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .stats__value {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stats__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  /* Sections */
  .section-heading {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .lead-text {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .feature-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .feature-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .feature-list li::before {
    content: '✓';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent-violet);
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  .gallery-grid {
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .gallery-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .phone-frame {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 320px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
    border: 8px solid #1a1a2e;
    background: #1a1a2e;
  }

  .phone-frame img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .gallery-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .spotbook-quote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-violet);
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-violet) 5%, var(--bg-cream));
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
  }

  /* Architecture */
  .arch-box, .arch-detail {
    padding: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-cream-dark);
    border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker);
  }

  .arch-box h3, .arch-detail h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .arch-detail p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .zone-list {
    list-style: none;
  }

  .zone-list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Capabilities */
  .capability-card {
    background: var(--bg-cream);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker);
    transition: transform var(--transition-base), box-shadow var(--transition-base);
  }

  .capability-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .capability-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .capability-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .capability-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Lessons */
  .lesson-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .lesson-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .lesson-card {
    background: var(--bg-cream);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--bg-cream-darker);
  }

  .lesson-card h4 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--accent-violet);
  }

  .lesson-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Honest callout */
  .honest-callout {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-coral) 8%, var(--bg-cream));
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-coral);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-lg) var(--radius-lg) 0;
  }

  .honest-callout h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--accent-coral);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .honest-callout p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .honest-callout p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
